.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="kappa_2(A) = sigma_max / sigma_min bounds how much a relative perturbation of the data can grow in the solution of A x = b, whichever algorithm solves it: expect to lose about log10(kappa) digits. The same number explains why least squares through the normal equations A^T A x = A^T b is fragile -- kappa(A^T A) = kappa(A)^2 -- while QR works with kappa(A) itself.">

