.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Truncating the SVD A = U diag(S) V^T to its k largest singular values gives the best rank-``k`` approximation of A: its error is sqrt(sigma_{k+1}^2 + ...) in the Frobenius norm and sigma_{k+1} in the spectral norm, and no other rank-``k`` matrix does better. The SVD itself comes from numpy.linalg.svd (LAPACK&#x27;s stable bidiagonalization route, not the eigendecomposition of A^T A).">

